-- title:
--   Fricke involution on Ogg's modular unit over ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a natural number carrying the instance asserting that it is prime, and write $u =$ `modularUnitSeries ℓ` for the rational Laurent series $\Delta \cdot (\Delta^{(\ell)})^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is `deltaSeries`, the product of $q$ with the $q$-expansion of the Dedekind eta unit, and $\Delta^{(\ell)}$ is its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$. Assume $u$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ`, the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the series $j(q^{d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $\ell$. Let `coeffEmb` denote the coefficientwise ring homomorphism $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let `modularFunctionFieldBar ℓ` be the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ` under `coeffEmb`; thus `coeffEmb` of $u$ is an element of it. The assertion is that applying `frickeInvolutionBar ℓ` — the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldBar ℓ` obtained from the $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism `frickeInvolutionFull ℓ` by the base-change homomorphism `geomAut` — to this element yields, as a Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, the scalar multiple by $(\ell : \bar{\mathbb{Q}})^{12}$ of the inverse of `coeffEmb` of $u$.
--
--   This is the behaviour of Ogg's modular unit $u = \Delta(z)/\Delta(\ell z)$ on $X_0(\ell)$ under the Fricke involution $w_\ell$, namely $w_\ell(u) = \ell^{12}u^{-1}$, transported from the field of modular functions over $\mathbb{Q}$ to its base change to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. It feeds the computations with the cuspidal divisor class and the order of $u$ at the two cusps, and is used in the level-one place-specialisation arguments concerning $u$ and $u^{-1}$.
